Spec179 dependency patch (applied only in the isolated NAC-ABE checkout)

Purpose: make identity DKEY renewal safe for grant-only Controller updates and
coalesce repeated refresh requests.

src/consumer.hpp:

    uint64_t m_cacheGeneration = 0;
    uint64_t m_dkeyGeneration = 0;
    bool m_dkeyFetchInFlight = false;
    bool m_dkeyFetchPending = false;

    void refreshDecryptionKey();

src/consumer.cpp, Consumer::obtainDecryptionKey():

* Return without publishing a second DKEY Interest when one fetch is already
  in flight; remember a pending request instead.
* Capture the DKEY-only generation at fetch start.
* Decode a complete replacement DKEY into a local object and assign it only
  after successful decode. A grant-only refresh therefore leaves the old key
  usable until the replacement is complete.
* Ignore a completion from an invalidated DKEY generation and issue at most one
  follow-up fetch when a pending refresh was requested.
* Clear in-flight/pending state on completion, error, or fetch-start failure.

This patch does not rotate the ABE master secret or public parameters. The
Controller's grant-only path replaces the target identity's complete policy;
`refreshDecryptionKey()` advances a DKEY-only fence and the next DKEY Interest
is generated from that policy by NAC-ABE. Withdrawal continues to use the
separate global generation-rotation path.

